      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FEAZABEEL (1) made it four wins from his last five runs, all at the mile, when he easily took out a BM75 at Canberra eight days ago. Although coming to the provincials this doesn't look as tough. Getting up in the weights but it is hard to tip against him. TOUSSAINT (8) enjoyed the step up to 1600m last time out when second-up from a spell, getting home by the barest margin at Goulburn. Up in grade but drops 4kgs and will improve further at just the third run back. Definite contender. Veteran SATNESS (3) hits his right race at the fifth run of the campaign. Boasts four wins and three placings from nine runs over the Kembla mile. Cannot be underestimated. ERINA (5) tackles a better race today after stringing two together. Not to be taken lightly.",
